Package: cellucid
Type: Package
Title: Prepare and View Single-Cell Data in the Cellucid Viewer
Version: 0.9.5
Config/cellucid/version-marker: CELLUCID_VERSION
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Kemal", "Inecik",
      email = "k.inecik@gmail.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
  )
Description: Writes single-cell embeddings, cell and gene metadata, gene
    expression, neighbour graphs, and vector fields as a 'Cellucid'-ready
    'AnnData' store: a standard 'AnnData' 'Zarr' store, as a folder or as one
    ZIP file, with gene-major expression and the dataset's name, citation and
    launch defaults, which the 'Cellucid' web viewer opens directly and the
    Python 'anndata' package reads. The primary entry point is
    cellucid_prepare(); cellucid_transition_drift() computes a vector field
    from a cell-cell transition matrix. cellucid_view() and cellucid_serve()
    open a 'Seurat', 'SingleCellExperiment' or 'SummarizedExperiment' object,
    or a file, in the 'Cellucid' viewer from a local 'httpuv' web server,
    with commands and events over a 'WebSocket'; the viewer's web
    application is downloaded from <https://www.cellucid.com> at first use
    and kept in the user's cache folder.
